While a neat idea, it wouldn't add much to the game as-is because your
wand of alchemy can produce only one type of item. Likely, that item
is useless, and in case it isn't, the potential for abuse is there.
This is a bit similar to the reason the alchemized blessed potion of
full healing has a bad rep among people worried about NetHack game
balance.

That said, manipulating material is certainly a neat idea. What
happens if you allow players to forge a tin and a copper wand into a
(recharged) bronze wand? What about combining certain valueable gems
and gold rings to make other rings?

There is a color alchemy patch.

Also, artifacts can be polymorphed, they just resist 95% of the time.


